    <section class="science-intro">
        <h1>Have you got something interesting?</h1>

        <h2>Let's test it.</h2>

        <p>
            Borderbio works with farmers, businesses, universities and research
            organisations to investigate agricultural products, research questions
            and new ideas.
        </p>
    </section>
<section class="science-section">
    <h2>Testing agricultural products and amendments</h2>

    <p>
        We can investigate a wide range of agricultural amendments, including
        plant extracts, biological products, fertilisers and soil conditioners.
    </p>

    <p>
        Depending on the question, this can include measuring effects on soil
        biology, nutrient availability and crop response, with controlled
        experiments used to determine whether a treatment produces a meaningful effect.
    </p>
</section>
<section class="science-section">
    <h2>Collaborative research</h2>

    <p>
        Borderbio is open to collaborative research with universities,
        research organisations, agricultural businesses and farmers where
        our interests and capabilities overlap.
    </p>

    <p>
        We are particularly interested in projects that connect laboratory
        investigation with practical agricultural questions and provide
        opportunities to test promising ideas under controlled and field conditions.
    </p>
</section>
<section class="science-section">
    <h2>Grant-funded R&amp;D</h2>

    <p>
        Borderbio is interested in developing collaborative research and
        development projects through agricultural innovation and other
        grant-funding programmes.
    </p>

    <p>
        We welcome opportunities to join or develop projects where our
        scientific capabilities, agricultural setting and experimental
        approach can contribute to answering a useful research question.
    </p>
</section>
<section class="work-section">
    <h2>Tell us what you're trying to find out.</h2>
